We have identified the allowance for expected credit losses as a key audit matter due to the significance of the loans and advances to the financial statements, the inherent complexity of the Company’s ECL models used to measure ECL allowances.
As part of an audit in accordance with SAs, we exercise professional judgement and maintain professional scepticism throughout the audit. We also:
• Recalculating the ECL on sample basis, by using the key assumptions used in the models, such as PD and LGD;
• Working with internal specialists in order to assess the management computation of ECL model including staging, PD, LGD, and appropriateness of incorporating the forward-looking factors, and assumptions to the ECL model;
